### 1475. Final Prices With a Special Discount in a Shop

**Problem:** For each item, subtract the price of the first item to its right whose price is less than or equal to its own price.

**Platform:** LeetCode
**Topic:** Array 

### Approach

For each `prices[i]`:

* Check every element to its right.
* Find the **first** `prices[j] <= prices[i]`.
* Apply the discount and stop searching.
* If no such element exists, keep the original price.

### Complexity

* **Time:** O(n²)
* **Space:** O(n)

### Code


class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> finalPrices(vector<int>& prices) {
        int n = prices.size();
        vector<int> ans(n);

        ans[n - 1] = prices[n - 1];

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            ans[i] = prices[i];

            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                if (prices[j] <= prices[i]) {
                    ans[i] = prices[i] - prices[j];
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
